# SECURITY — XSS, CSP, third-party network
File: website/audit/security.oot

Verdict: PASS on stored HTML injection and reduced motion
after the 2026-09-04 repair. Residual: email collect origin
and the install.sh pipe.

## 1. simpleMarkdown (Red 4)

`src/route/markdown.js` escapes the whole body with
`escapeHtml` before markdown replacements. There is no
RAWHTML preserve. Title, source, and error text use
`escapeHtml`. Table rule-rows (`|---|`) emit nothing.

A `<script>` tag in a pulled `.oot` file becomes text.

## 2. Content-Security-Policy

`index.html` and `404.html` set:

  default-src 'self'
  script-src 'self'
  style-src 'self'
  connect-src 'self' https://collect.openooda.org
  form-action https://collect.openooda.org

Theme boot lives in `src/theme/boot.js`. No `unsafe-inline`.
No Google Fonts. System monospace stack in `styles/main.css`.

## 3. Email collect

The join form POSTs to https://collect.openooda.org/v1/emails.
Honeypot field `website` is present. `credentials: omit`.
This origin is a product choice. Do not delete it in this
repo without an owner decision.

## 4. install.sh pipe to bash

`website/install.sh` curls packaging `install.sh` and pipes
to bash. Keep the URL. Do not add more shell.

## 5. Reduced motion

`CanvasLifecycleManager` gates rAF. Sky and dogfight both
register `respectReducedMotion: true`. CSS hides `#sky` and
`#dogfight-canvas` under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
`initGlobalDogfight` does not set an inline `display` and
does not force `start()` after register.

## 6. Next repair

Document the collect.openooda.org data retained, or delete
the form, as an owner decision. Not this pass.
